  "body": "## Summary\n\nMaintainers currently decide and run server, native and OTA releases separately, which makes unnecessary builds and uncertain retries difficult to avoid. This prepares one manual **Release changed artifacts** entrypoint that compares immutable inputs with each artifact's last verified success, proposes versions and runs only the required existing workers.\n\nThe plan preserves Android phone/Wear allocation, exact-candidate CI, signed tags and image receipts. It adds independent iOS build allocation and IPA verification, compatible per-runtime OTA, and durable recovery without blindly repeating uncertain provider requests. Production approval precedes OTA environment resolution, export and publication. Backend/project/profile settings are supplied externally at build time. iOS upload inputs are prepared separately; TestFlight processing and production rollout are not claimed.\n\nRefs #447. **Review order: PR441, then this child.** Actual target: `mchartier/release-entrypoints-recovery` at `cd8932b2`; source parent: `0c26cea`; ultimate target: `master` at `547206a`. PR441 is preserved. Managed-hosted PR450 is a separate proposed integration dependency; its changes are not included or claimed implemented here.\n\n## Test plan and behavior evidence\n\nThis is non-UI release tooling. The evidence is [actual synthetic CLI/JSON plans, worker arguments and state transitions](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/80703680c484c534bcfa0f7ee18760870d2acc6f/behavior.json), with [reproduction and full evidence](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/80703680c484c534bcfa0f7ee18760870d2acc6f/README.md).\n\n| Starting state and action | Expected and observed |\n| --- | --- |\n| All verified artifact inputs match; execute the plan | No stages and zero journal/candidate/provider writes. |\n| Change only server, either native platform, or either compatible bundle | Select only the corresponding stage; OTA retains the installed native runtime. |\n| Change server and both native inputs | Allocate paired Android and independent iOS versions, then run server last through its original candidate/image gates. |\n| Lose a provider response, then retry twice | Retain intent, reconcile one operation and reuse its verified result; one provider start total. |\n| Retry OTA with an empty provider inventory | Reject another publication. Changed native/configuration/export/channel identities also reject in maintained regressions. |\n| Cancel the handler before plan persistence, then start the next run | Actual workflow jobs pass through the GitHub adapter; retirement retains a tombstone and permits the next allocation. Lost provider responses retain their intent and remain blocked. |\n| Inspect the production OTA job graph without dispatching | The existing environment approval gates resolution; export, intent and publication each require the preceding job to succeed. Source export has no provider credentials. |\n| Prepare iOS delivery | Build arguments freeze existing credentials; upload arguments select an exact verified store build. Neither command was executed against a provider. |\n\n[Actual-path recovery and approval-order evidence](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/517fd4b8f69a67e6e7e50f251b656849efe05556/qa-corrections.json) includes rejected unknown/missing phases, successful earlier execution and interrupted cleanup. Maintained fixtures additionally cover stale source, missing/failed CI, incompatible OTA, partial completion, conflicting receipts, concurrency and interrupted cleanup with retained tombstones/readback.\n\n## Supporting checks and limitations\n\nRelease tests recorded at unchanged head `50f4a845`: **278 passed, 2 existing skips**; **71 focused recovery/workflow tests passed**, and release consistency checks passed. The prior native-release, operations, Wear unit and deployment results remain applicable to unchanged code. All five hosted workflows at that head passed, including Android debug and iOS simulator compilation. Their recorded base is `0c26cea`; they do not validate an integrated build against today's target or master. Migration and opt-in emulator/UI jobs remain skipped.\n\nRaw actionlint 1.7.12 remains **not clean**: the affected OTA workflow has only its existing `queue: max` schema diagnostic. The [full original comparison](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/80703680c484c534bcfa0f7ee18760870d2acc6f/actionlint-compatibility.json) retains 61 inherited and seven added diagnostics for documented GitHub Cloud features; no broad suppression was added.\n\nSource: `50f4a845`. The [complete published scope](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/517fd4b8f69a67e6e7e50f251b656849efe05556/qa-corrections-scope.json) binds four focused commits and 86 files. Actual PR merge-base/source parent is `0c26cea`; `4cbcbc7` is the ultimate-master merge-base. The two-file documentation delta to actual target `cd8932b2` remains conflict-free, with a byte-identical integrated child patch. The [ultimate-target impact assessment](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/blob/d7d8e07195c625bf7e0fbad046b1c9372dec5b5b/ultimate-refresh-impact.json) covers the subsequent `9dc0739` \u2192 `547206a` authentication/goal changes: 29 paths do not overlap this child's diff, and non-committing conflict probes preserve that incoming delta exactly. Backend changes will affect server input identity on a future plan; native/OTA selectors and configuration are unchanged. No new tests or integrated runtime validation were performed for this metadata refresh. Historical evidence remains bound to its recorded sources. Detailed evidence and original descriptions remain on a separate nonmerged ref.\n\nThe configured Codex review [refused solely for review quota](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/pull/452#issuecomment-6070337167); no bot review is claimed or retried. The [published independent assessment](https://github.com/MChartier/calibrate-health/pull/452#issuecomment-6071694756) resolved R1/R2 and verified 89 affected/adjacent tests, code, behavior and evidence against its recorded head/base/body; its historical ultimate-master binding is `9dc0739`. No actual release, paid build, credential setup, provider upload/publication, deployment or device installation occurred. Real IPA/provider validation and native-device checks remain unrun.",
